<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>18 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta), Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>14 - Abel Balbo (Roma)</p>
<p>13 - Roberto Mancini (Sampdoria), Sandro Tovalieri (Cagliari)</p>
<p>12 - Youri Djorkaeff (Inter), Marcelo Otero (Vicenza)</p>
<p>11 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna),</p>
<p>Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>10 - Marcio Amoroso (Udinese), Enrico Chiesa (Parma), Filippo</p>
<p>Maniero (Verona), George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p>9 - Marco Negri (Perugia), Oliver Bierhoff (Udinese), Pasquale</p>
<p>Luiso (Piacenza), Paolo Poggi (Udinese)</p>
<p>8 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Alessandro Del Piero and</p>
<p>Michele Padovano (both Juventus)</p>
<p>7 - Hernan Crespo (Parma), Roberto Muzzi (Cagliari), Anselmo</p>
<p>Robbiati (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>6 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Kennet Andersson (Bologna),</p>
<p>Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria), Maurizio Ganz (Inter), Roberto</p>
<p>Murgita (Vicenza), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>5 - Roberto Baggio (Milan), Marco Branca and Ivan Zamorano</p>
<p>(both Inter), Nicola Caccia, Andre Cruz and Fabio Pecchia (all</p>
<p>Napoli), Giampiero Maini (Vicenza), Domenico Morfeo (Atalanta),</p>
<p>Pierluigi Orlandini and Antonio De Vitis (both Verona), Igor</p>
<p>Simutenkov (Reggiana), Christian Vieri (Juventus)</p>
</text>
